From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: mods found when bare_app runs the client are active

On the ODROID-GO Advance the game files, mods included, are copied from
a PC to a FAT32 partition, and the board has no launcher to turn a mod
on: VCMI only adds the mods its launcher installs to the preset, so a
copied mod stayed off. When bare_app runs the client (BARE_APP_LANG, as
in 0001) every installed root mod is added to the active preset unless
it asks to stay off (keepDisabled). Removing its directory turns it off.
Translation mods of another language still do not load (0001).
---
 lib/modding/ModManager.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/modding/ModManager.cpp b/lib/modding/ModManager.cpp
index 986a631..de7f0ef 100644
--- a/lib/modding/ModManager.cpp
+++ b/lib/modding/ModManager.cpp
@@ -610,6 +610,16 @@ void ModManager::addNewModsToPreset()
 {
 	const TModList & installedMods = getInstalledValidMods();
 
+	// Started by bare_app: the game files are copied from a PC and nothing
+	// on the board turns mods on or off, so every mod installed is active
+	// unless it asks to stay off. Removing its directory turns it off.
+	if(std::getenv("BARE_APP_LANG"))
+	{
+		for(const auto & modID : installedMods)
+			if(modID.find('.') == std::string::npos && !modsStorage->getMod(modID).keepDisabled())
+				modsPreset->addRootMod(modID);
+	}
+
 	for(const auto & modID : installedMods)
 	{
 		size_t dotPos = modID.find('.');
